## Cloudflare's sign-in, by the owner
INFO  first try: the owner authorized about 12 minutes after the link was made. Cloudflare's page said
      "Success", but the tunnel kept logging "Waiting for login...". Not cloudflare/cloudflared#1252: no
      file was saved in the browser. The link had run out: cloudflared's login polls ten times, about 53 s
      each, then exits, and the service starts a new login with a new link (the page shows the new one; the
      link was relayed by hand here, so the owner used the old one).
INFO  the next login's link lasted 17 s before another replaced it (its log is overwritten on restart, so
      why isn't known); the one after that held
PASS  second try, on the current link: cloudflare-state is running within a minute of authorizing (20:50:53 UTC)
PASS  https://<name C>/_liveness answers ok 7 s later
PASS  no Cloudflare sign-in (.cloudflared/, cert.pem) is kept. data/cloudflare holds: routed 27 B, tunnel-name 18 B, tunnel.token 181 B

